BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sphera-media-lab-2026-open-call-discourse@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260824T105311Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260831
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
SUMMARY:Deadline: Sphera Media Lab 2026: Open Call for Masterclasses and Ke
 ynotes
DESCRIPTION:European Lab and the Sphera Network are opening submissions for
  the discourse programme of the next Sphera Media Lab\, the annual forum f
 or people defending independent media in Europe. THEMES: technological ind
 ependence (sovereignty\, tools\, mutualisation)\; economic independence (c
 ooperative models)\; editorial independence (press freedom\, resisting the
  far right). FORMATS SOUGHT: masterclasses\, led by an expert sharing adva
 nced knowledge\, technique and hands-on insight\; and keynotes\, inspiring
  talks grounded in a specific case study. WHO CAN PROPOSE: media outlets\,
  associations\, researchers and professionals. The organisers state they p
 ay particular attention to parity and diversity across their programmes an
 d ask that proposals take those criteria into account. WHAT IS COVERED: se
 lected contributors travel to Brussels with transport\, accommodation and 
 a fee covered. THE EVENT: Sphera Media Lab 2026 runs on 3 December 2026 at
  LaVallee in Brussels\, a full day of conferences\, masterclasses and work
 shops for independent media professionals from across Europe\, alongside t
 he premiere of a documentary on threats facing European journalists. APPLI
 CATION: submit your masterclass or keynote proposal via the Typeform at ar
 ty-farty.typeform.com/to/xnDikGGM before 31 August 2026.\n\nOrganisation: 
 European Lab (Arty Farty) and the Sphera Network\, coordinated by Medianes
 \nLocation: LaVallee\, Rue Adolphe Lavallee 39\, 1080 Brussels\, Belgium. 
 Proposals are accepted regardless of where you are based\, but they should
  reflect a European perspective.\nAward: Selected contributors receive a f
 ee plus travel to Brussels and accommodation\, all covered by the organise
 rs. The fee amount is not published in the call. No submission fee.\nDurat
 ion: One-day event on 3 December 2026\; contributors deliver a single mast
 erclass or keynote\n\nMore: https://arty-farty.typeform.com/to/xnDikGGM?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://arty-farty.typeform.com/to/xnDikGGM?utm_source=artificialnouvea
 ugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:LaVallee\, Rue Adolphe Lavallee 39\, 1080 Brussels\, Belgium. Prop
 osals are accepted regardless of where you are based\, but they should ref
 lect a European perspective.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:american-academy-berlin-prize-2027-28@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260824T105311Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260925
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260926
SUMMARY:Deadline: American Academy in Berlin: Berlin Prize Fellowship 2027-
 28
DESCRIPTION:The American Academy in Berlin is an independent\, nonprofit in
 stitute for advanced study in the arts\, humanities\, social sciences\, la
 w\, journalism and public policy\, whose primary mission is to strengthen 
 the cultural and intellectual ties between the United States and Germany. 
 Each year\, after a rigorous selection process\, the Academy awards roughl
 y two dozen semester-long Berlin Prize fellowships to individuals who demo
 nstrate excellence in their fields. DISCIPLINES: applications are welcome 
 across the humanities\, social sciences\, law\, journalism and various are
 as of public policy. The Academy generally encourages projects addressing 
 pressing issues of the day\, specifically naming democracy\, security\, te
 chnology and society (especially AI)\, energy including climate\, and glob
 al order. Dedicated fellowships also support projects in Jewish studies\, 
 German studies\, and public health and biotechnology. Project proposals ne
 ed not focus on Germany\, but candidates should explain how a residency in
  Berlin would enhance their work. NOT ACCEPTED: proposals in mathematics o
 r the natural sciences. NOTE FOR ARTISTS: visual artists and composers are
  invited through separate\, nomination-based competitions\, so there is no
  open application route for them here. ELIGIBILITY: fellowships are restri
 cted to citizens and permanent residents of the United States. Both emergi
 ng and established figures are eligible. PhD holders qualify as emerging s
 cholars with a strong record of peer-reviewed work beyond the dissertation
 \; candidates in non-academic fields such as journalism\, filmmaking and p
 olicy need a significant record of publication or production\; fiction and
  nonfiction writers must have published at least one book with a reputable
  press. WHAT FELLOWS DO: fellows present their work to audiences in and ar
 ound Berlin through lectures\, readings\, public discussions\, performance
 s and film screenings\, and should be willing to engage with relevant Germ
 an institutions\, organizations and the media\; these activities are integ
 ral to the Academy's mission of fostering transatlantic dialogue. APPLICAT
 ION MATERIALS: a project proposal of 1\,500 to 1\,750 words plus a one-pag
 e bibliography\; a curriculum vitae of up to 10 pages\; two writing sample
 s totalling no more than 60 pages\; and three letters of recommendation\, 
 which are due 2 October 2026. DEADLINE: Friday 25 September 2026 at 12:00 
 noon Eastern Time (18:00 Central European Time). TIMELINE: all candidates 
 are notified of the competition outcome by email in late March 2027\; the 
 2027-28 Berlin Prize recipients are announced in May 2027.\n\nOrganisation
 : American Academy in Berlin\nLocation: Berlin\, Germany\, at the Hans Arn
 hold Center. RESTRICTED: fellowships are open only to citizens and permane
 nt residents of the United States.\nAward: Monthly stipend of USD 5\,000\,
  plus roundtrip airfare\, accommodation at or near the Hans Arnhold Center
 \, partial board\, in-house library services and professional networking o
 pportunities. Roughly two dozen fellowships awarded each year. No applicat
 ion fee.\nDuration: One full academic semester (about 4 months). Fall runs
  mid-August to mid-December\; spring runs late January to late May.\n\nMor
 e: https://www.americanacademy.de/apply/apply-for-a-fellowship/?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.americanacademy.de/apply/apply-for-a-fellowship/?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Berlin\, Germany\, at the Hans Arnhold Center. RESTRICTED: fellows
 hips are open only to citizens and permanent residents of the United State
 s.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ditrapano-finch-manuscript-lab-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260824T105311Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260710
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260711
SUMMARY:Deadline: Giancarlo DiTrapano Foundation: The Finch Manuscript Lab 
 2026
DESCRIPTION:The Finch Manuscript Lab is a 2.5-month residency supporting wr
 iters completing book-length manuscripts\, hosted at the Finch Country Hou
 se in Serramezzana\, Italy\, and designed as the final sprint in the marat
 hon of writing a book. It offers living and work space\, writing time in a
  tranquil setting\, creative community\, and professional development incl
 uding manuscript consultations\, craft discussions\, and publishing semina
 rs. Residency dates: 1 October to 15 December 2026\; residents will be sel
 ected by 30 July 2026. FUNDING: thanks to the support of the Goethe Instit
 ute and Culture Moves Europe\, all selected residents receive a stipend of
  EUR 2\,280 for the residency period (EUR 30 per day in residence\, paid w
 eekly)\, a travel allowance of EUR 400 for distances under 5\,000 km from 
 Serramezzana or EUR 800 for distances over 5\,000 km\, an additional EUR 4
 00 for green travel (e.g. taking trains instead of planes)\, and additiona
 l support of EUR 200 for parents of children under 18. ELIGIBILITY: applic
 ants must be over 18 and a legal resident of one of the 39 Culture Moves E
 urope eligible countries\, excluding Italy\; this includes all EU member s
 tates other than Italy and 13 participating non-EU countries (Albania\, An
 dorra\, Armenia\, Bosnia and Herzegovina\, Georgia\, Iceland\, Kosovo\, Mo
 ldova\, Montenegro\, North Macedonia\, Norway\, Serbia\, and Tunisia). APP
 LICATION (via Submittable\, in order of importance): a short sample of pas
 t work (any length\, though only the first 30 pages may be read)\; a brief
  note\, up to one page\, explaining the manuscript or book project to be w
 orked on in residency\, where you are in the creation process\, and why yo
 u are interested\; an excerpt of the book project not exceeding 30 pages (
 prose\, poetry\, mixed media\, photography\, or any other form of artist's
  book is acceptable)\; and a CV in English. NOTE ON DEADLINE: the foundati
 on's text gives the open call as 15 June to 10 July 2026\, while the Submi
 ttable page lists a close of Wednesday 15 July 2026 at 12:00 PM\; apply by
  10 July to be safe.\n\nOrganisation: The Giancarlo DiTrapano Foundation f
 or Literature and the Arts\nLocation: Finch Country House\, Serramezzana\,
  Italy\; open to legal residents of the 39 Culture Moves Europe eligible c
 ountries\, excluding Italy\nAward: EUR 2\,280 stipend for the residency pe
 riod (EUR 30 per day in residence\, paid weekly)\, plus travel allowance o
 f EUR 400 (under 5\,000 km) or EUR 800 (over 5\,000 km)\, an additional EU
 R 400 green-travel top-up (e.g. trains instead of planes)\, and EUR 200 ad
 ditional support for parents of children under 18. Supported by the Goethe
  Institute and Culture Moves Europe.\nDuration: 2.5 months\, 1 October to 
 15 December 2026\n\nMore: https://ditrapanofoundation.submittable.com/subm
 it/171cc54d-b582-47a3-93a4-47c46b65904b/the-finch-manuscript-lab?utm_sourc
 e=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://ditrapanofoundation.submittable.com/submit/171cc54d-b582-47a3-9
 3a4-47c46b65904b/the-finch-manuscript-lab?utm_source=artificialnouveaugran
 tdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Finch Country House\, Serramezzana\, Italy\; open to legal residen
 ts of the 39 Culture Moves Europe eligible countries\, excluding Italy
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:page-not-found-neu-commission-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260824T105311Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260731
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260801
SUMMARY:Deadline: NEU Commission 2026
DESCRIPTION:Page Not Found announces the third edition of the NEU Commissio
 n\, which intends to support the emergence of alternative voices within co
 ntemporary art. It targets a group currently under-represented in Europe: 
 art students with limited financial means who are required to provide a gu
 arantee for their visa and to pay high non-EU tuition fees\, economical ba
 rriers to their participation in art and knowledge production in The Nethe
 rlands. Page Not Found will commission three art students from non-Europea
 n countries to each write an essay or a free-form text in English. Each se
 lected writer receives EUR 2\,000 for the commission\, provided as an adva
 nce payment in September 2026\; the commissioned texts are published at a 
 later date. OPEN CALL: only students enrolled in Dutch art academies who a
 re NOT nationals of the European Economic Area are eligible. The commissio
 ned text does not need to be submitted when answering the open call\; the 
 jury selects recipients based on their previous writing and financial need
 . Review the Rules of the Open Call and the FAQ before applying. Deadline:
  Friday 31 July 2026\, 23:59 CEST (Amsterdam).\n\nOrganisation: Page Not F
 ound\nLocation: The Netherlands\; open to non-EEA-national students enroll
 ed at Dutch art academies.\nAward: EUR 2\,000 each to three commissioned w
 riters\, paid as an advance in September 2026.\nDuration: One-time commiss
 ion\; commissioned texts published at a later date\n\nMore: http://neu-com
 mission.page-not-found.nl/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_mediu
 m=referral
URL:http://neu-commission.page-not-found.nl/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:The Netherlands\; open to non-EEA-national students enrolled at Du
 tch art academies.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:translation-house-looren-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260824T105311Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
SUMMARY:Deadline: Translation House Looren: Translators' Residencies and Pr
 o Helvetia Stipends 2027
DESCRIPTION:Translators' residency at Uebersetzerhaus Looren in Wernetshaus
 en near Zurich. Looren offers a free residency for literary translators wi
 th a current contract\, including six competitive CHF 4\,000 stipend grant
 s per year tied to one-month residencies. The Pro Helvetia residency progr
 amme (separately funded) has a 2026-10-15 deadline for 2027 stays. The Jam
 es Joyce Scholarship and Looren Residency 2027 closes 2026-10-31. General 
 free residencies are accepted on a rolling basis throughout the year. ELIG
 IBILITY: literary translators with substantial published work and a curren
 t translation contract\; any language combination is welcome. Apply via th
 e application page on looren.net. No application fee.\n\nOrganisation: Ueb
 ersetzerhaus Looren\nLocation: Wernetshausen\, Switzerland (Zurich region)
 \nAward: Free residency stay (apartments at the translation house). Six co
 mpetitive CHF 4\,000 translation grants per year\, each tied to a one-mont
 h residency. Pro Helvetia residency programme separately funded. James Joy
 ce Scholarship and Looren Residency 2027 has its own conditions. No applic
 ation fee.\nDuration: Stays of typically 2 weeks to 2 months\; CHF 4\,000 
 stipend grants tied to one-month residencies\n\nMore: https://looren.net/e
 n/residencies/application-for-a-stay?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
URL:https://looren.net/en/residencies/application-for-a-stay?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Wernetshausen\, Switzerland (Zurich region)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:letterenfonds-project-grants-translators@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260824T105311Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260816
SUMMARY:Deadline: Nederlands Letterenfonds: Project Grants for Literary Tra
 nslators (August 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:Project subsidies from the Nederlands Letterenfonds for advance
 d literary translators with a current publishing contract for a translatio
 n from or into Dutch. The next round closes 15 August 2026\; decisions are
  made approximately four months after the deadline (December). ELIGIBILITY
 : literary translators with a substantial published portfolio and a contra
 cted translation project\; primary income must be below EUR 52\,500.\n\nOr
 ganisation: Nederlands Letterenfonds (Dutch Foundation for Literature)\nLo
 cation: Worldwide (literary translators with a contracted translation from
  or into Dutch)\nAward: Project-based subsidy. Income cap EUR 52\,500 for 
 primary income. Standard minimum rates: EUR 0.0802/word for prose\; EUR 2.
 92/line for poetry. No application fee.\nDuration: Project-based\, scaled 
 to the contracted translation\n\nMore: https://www.letterenfonds.nl/en-car
 ibbean/funding/project-grants-for-literary-translators?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.letterenfonds.nl/en-caribbean/funding/project-grants-for-li
 terary-translators?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referr
 al
LOCATION:Worldwide (literary translators with a contracted translation from
  or into Dutch)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jan-michalski-foundation-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260824T105311Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260831
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
SUMMARY:Deadline: Jan Michalski Foundation: Writers Residency 2027
DESCRIPTION:Residency for writers and translators at the Jan Michalski Foun
 dation in Montricher\, Switzerland\, set in seven distinctive 'cabin' modu
 les hanging from an openwork canopy\, offering conditions to start\, conti
 nue or finish a writing project. Around forty authors from around the worl
 d (emerging to established) are hosted each year. Open to all kinds of wri
 ting and all languages\, with priority given to literary writers and trans
 lators\; other disciplines are welcome as long as literature is at the hea
 rt of the project. Residencies are for individuals or pairs working on a c
 ommon project (e.g. a writer and a translator). A percentage of residencie
 s are dedicated to nature writing. WHAT IS PROVIDED: a private cabin for i
 ndependent living (a separate cabin per person for pairs\; one accessible 
 cabin for reduced mobility)\, travel costs to and from home\, a weekly all
 owance of CHF 400\, breakfast and lunch\, electric bikes\, and daytime lib
 rary access. ELIGIBILITY: no age or nationality restrictions\; beginners a
 ccepted\; one application per year\; former residents may not reapply (fam
 ilies\, children and pets cannot be accommodated). Stays cannot be split i
 nto multiple periods. Selection is by a panel chaired by Vera Michalski-Ho
 ffmann\, assessing the literary quality of the project\, the candidate's b
 ackground\, and whether the stay length matches the project scope. APPLICA
 TION: online in English or French (work excerpts may be in any language)\;
  the 2027 form is open 2 June to 31 August 2026\; selected candidates anno
 unced December 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Jan Michalski Foundation for Writing
  and Literature\nLocation: Montricher\, Switzerland (Swiss Jura\, near Lau
 sanne and Geneva)\nAward: Weekly allowance of CHF 400\, plus travel costs 
 to and from home covered\, accommodation in a private cabin\, and breakfas
 t and lunch provided. Electric bikes and library access included.\nDuratio
 n: Two weeks to three months (first 2027 residents arrive mid-January 2027
 )\n\nMore: https://fondation-janmichalski.com/en/residences?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://fondation-janmichalski.com/en/residences?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Montricher\, Switzerland (Swiss Jura\, near Lausanne and Geneva)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:hubert-butler-essay-prize-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260824T105311Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260703
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260704
SUMMARY:Deadline: Hubert Butler Essay Prize 2026
DESCRIPTION:Annual essay prize for a previously unpublished essay of up to 
 3\,000 words on a set theme. The 2026 theme takes Auden's line 'Poetry mak
 es nothing happen' as a prompt about what impact high culture can have in 
 a world facing crisis - well suited to a critical essayist working on AI\,
  media and society. Judged blind\, so it is open to and fair for debut wri
 ters (no publication history required). ELIGIBILITY: entrants must be over
  18 and a citizen of the UK or an EU member state. Deadline 3 July 2026.\n
 \nOrganisation: Hubert Butler Essay Prize (with Haus Publishing)\nLocation
 : Ireland (online submission)\nAward: EUR 2\,500 prize (sponsored by Haus 
 Publishing). No entry fee.\nDuration: Annual essay prize\n\nMore: https://
 www.hubertbutleressayprize.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_
 medium=referral
URL:https://www.hubertbutleressayprize.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Ireland (online submission)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stinging-fly-creative-nonfiction-submissions@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20260824T105311Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261123
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261124
SUMMARY:Deadline: The Stinging Fly: Open Submissions (Creative Nonfiction)
DESCRIPTION:Leading Irish literary magazine that publishes and pays for cre
 ative nonfiction (as well as fiction and poetry)\, with a stated particula
 r interest in promoting new and emerging writers. A clean\, no-fee\, inter
 nationally-open outlet for a standalone critical/creative-nonfiction piece
 . ELIGIBILITY: Irish and international writers\; debut-friendly\, no publi
 shed-book requirement. Submissions are accepted in specific windows\; the 
 next nonfiction window runs Monday 9 November to Monday 23 November 2026 (
 closes 5pm Irish time) for the Summer 2027 issue.\n\nOrganisation: The Sti
 nging Fly\nLocation: Dublin\, Ireland (international submissions)\nAward: 
 Paid on acceptance: nonfiction approx. EUR 50/page (minimum EUR 375\, maxi
 mum EUR 1\,250). No submission fee.\nDuration: Per piece\; submissions acc
 epted in timed windows\n\nMore: https://stingingfly.org/submissions/?utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://stingingfly.org/submissions/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Dublin\, Ireland (international submissions)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:prohelvetia-comic-creation-grant-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260824T105311Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Comic Creation Grant
DESCRIPTION:Pro Helvetia's comic creation grant supports the development of
  comic projects intended for publication\, including digital formats. Appl
 icants must have published at least one independent work with a profession
 al publisher or the equivalent in magazines. ELIGIBILITY: requires a conne
 ction to Switzerland (Swiss citizenship\, or permanent residency with regu
 lar artistic activity in Switzerland)\; not open to practitioners without 
 a Swiss connection. AMOUNT: maximum CHF 25\,000. Submission deadline 1 Sep
 tember (23:59 CEST). Apply via the Pro Helvetia portal.\n\nOrganisation: P
 ro Helvetia (Swiss Arts Council)\nLocation: Switzerland-based comic creato
 rs.\nAward: Maximum CHF 25\,000. No application fee.\nDuration: Creation p
 hase for a comic project intended for publication\; deadline 1 September.\
 n\nMore: https://prohelvetia.ch/en/find-support/comic-creation-grant?utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://prohelvetia.ch/en/find-support/comic-creation-grant?utm_source=
 artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Switzerland-based comic creators.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:prohelvetia-emerging-authors-frankfurter-seilschaften-2026@artificialno
 uveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260824T105311Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Emerging Authors: Frankfurter Seilschaften
DESCRIPTION:Frankfurter Seilschaften is a Pro Helvetia mentoring initiative
  pairing emerging Swiss literary practitioners with established authors du
 ring the Frankfurt Book Fair. To be eligible as an emerging author\, appli
 cants must have completed their artistic training or presented their work 
 publicly for the first time within the last five years\; the call also inc
 ludes professional writers who identify as FINTA. ELIGIBILITY: requires a 
 connection to Switzerland (Swiss citizenship\, or permanent residency with
  regular artistic activity in Switzerland)\; not open to practitioners wit
 hout a Swiss connection. WHAT IS OFFERED: hotel and travel expenses\, per 
 diems\, and trade fair passes. Submission deadline 1 September (23:59 CEST
 ). Apply via the Pro Helvetia portal.\n\nOrganisation: Pro Helvetia (Swiss
  Arts Council)\nLocation: Emerging authors with a connection to Switzerlan
 d\; also open to professional writers who identify as FINTA.\nAward: Hotel
  and travel expenses\, per diems\, and trade fair passes (amounts not spec
 ified). No application fee.\nDuration: Mentoring during the Frankfurt Book
  Fair\; deadline 1 September.\n\nMore: https://prohelvetia.ch/en/find-supp
 ort/emerging-authors-frankfurter-seilschaften?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://prohelvetia.ch/en/find-support/emerging-authors-frankfurter-sei
 lschaften?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Emerging authors with a connection to Switzerland\; also open to p
 rofessional writers who identify as FINTA.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:prohelvetia-literary-creation-grant-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260824T105311Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Literary Creation Grant
DESCRIPTION:Pro Helvetia's literary creation grant supports the development
  of literary projects intended for publication\, including fiction\, child
 ren's and youth literature\, poetry\, drama\, and spoken word. Applicants 
 must have prior published work\, a premiere\, or professional performances
 . ELIGIBILITY: requires a connection to Switzerland (Swiss citizenship\, o
 r permanent residency with regular artistic activity in Switzerland)\; not
  open to practitioners without a Swiss connection. AMOUNT: up to CHF 25\,0
 00 for writing\, CHF 18\,000 for theatre texts\, or CHF 15\,000 for perfor
 mative literary projects. Deadlines twice a year: 1 March (23:59 CET) and 
 1 September (23:59 CEST). Apply via the Pro Helvetia portal.\n\nOrganisati
 on: Pro Helvetia (Swiss Arts Council)\nLocation: Switzerland-based authors
  and collectives.\nAward: Up to CHF 25\,000 (writing)\, CHF 18\,000 (theat
 re texts)\, or CHF 15\,000 (performative literary projects). No applicatio
 n fee.\nDuration: Creation phase for a literary project intended for publi
 cation\; deadlines twice yearly (1 March and 1 September).\n\nMore: https:
 //prohelvetia.ch/en/find-support/literary-creation-grant?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://prohelvetia.ch/en/find-support/literary-creation-grant?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Switzerland-based authors and collectives.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:prohelvetia-writing-in-residency-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260824T105311Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Writing in Residency
DESCRIPTION:Pro Helvetia's Writing in Residency programme provides residenc
 y opportunities (for example Traduki in Southeast Europe or Art Omi) for a
 uthors and translators to develop or research projects. Applicants must ha
 ve prior professionally published work. ELIGIBILITY: requires a connection
  to Switzerland (Swiss citizenship\, or permanent residency with regular a
 rtistic activity in Switzerland)\; not open to practitioners without a Swi
 ss connection. WHAT IS OFFERED: travel and accommodation costs (varying by
  destination)\, plus childcare support of up to CHF 1\,000 per month for a
 pplicants with caregiving responsibilities. Submission deadline 1 Septembe
 r (23:59 CEST). Apply via the Pro Helvetia portal.\n\nOrganisation: Pro He
 lvetia (Swiss Arts Council)\nLocation: Switzerland-based authors and trans
 lators\; residencies at partner locations abroad (e.g. Traduki in Southeas
 t Europe\, Art Omi).\nAward: Travel and accommodation costs (vary by desti
 nation)\; childcare support up to CHF 1\,000 per month for applicants with
  caregiving responsibilities. No application fee.\nDuration: Residency to 
 develop or research a project\; deadline 1 September.\n\nMore: https://pro
 helvetia.ch/en/find-support/writing-in-residency?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://prohelvetia.ch/en/find-support/writing-in-residency?utm_source=
 artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Switzerland-based authors and translators\; residencies at partner
  locations abroad (e.g. Traduki in Southeast Europe\, Art Omi).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:prohelvetia-international-promotion-institutions-in-switzerland-2026@ar
 tificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260824T105311Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: International Promotion: Institutions in Switzerland (Lit
 erature)
DESCRIPTION:Pro Helvetia's international promotion grant (Switzerland-based
  institutions variant) funds the international promotion of contemporary S
 wiss literature through book fairs\, group publisher appearances\, and lit
 erary festivals. Open to event organizers\, publishing houses\, profession
 al associations\, and digital platforms based in Switzerland with regular 
 artistic activity there. ELIGIBILITY: requires a connection to Switzerland
  (Swiss citizenship\, or permanent residency with regular artistic activit
 y in Switzerland)\; not open to practitioners without a Swiss connection. 
 AMOUNT: maximum CHF 25\,000. Deadlines twice a year: 1 March (23:59 CET) a
 nd 1 September (23:59 CEST). Apply via the Pro Helvetia portal.\n\nOrganis
 ation: Pro Helvetia (Swiss Arts Council)\nLocation: Event organizers\, pub
 lishing houses\, professional associations\, and digital platforms based i
 n Switzerland.\nAward: Maximum CHF 25\,000. No application fee.\nDuration:
  Promotion project at book fairs\, festivals\, or literary events\; deadli
 nes twice yearly (1 March and 1 September).\n\nMore: https://prohelvetia.c
 h/en/find-support/international-promotion-2?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://prohelvetia.ch/en/find-support/international-promotion-2?utm_so
 urce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Event organizers\, publishing houses\, professional associations\,
  and digital platforms based in Switzerland.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fondsbjp-dossiersubsidie-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260824T105311Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260914
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260915
SUMMARY:Deadline: Fonds BJP: Dossiersubsidie for Freelance Regional and Loc
 al Journalists (autumn 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:The Dossiersubsidie is the Fonds BJP scheme for freelance regio
 nal and local journalists in the Netherlands who want to follow one subjec
 t properly rather than chase daily news\, funding up to EUR 19\,200 for si
 x months of sustained reporting on a single dossier. It is aimed at the ga
 p left by shrinking regional newsrooms\, where structural coverage of loca
 l government\, housing\, care or industry rarely gets paid time. ELIGIBILI
 TY: freelance journalists working in Dutch regional and local media only (
 staff journalists and national-only reporters are directed to the fund's o
 ther schemes). The fund also runs a year-round Vooronderzoekssubsidie of u
 p to EUR 8\,800 for preliminary research and a year-round Uitvoeringssubsi
 die of up to EUR 38\,600 for carrying out projects\, both open to all jour
 nalists. APPLICATION WINDOW: 17 August to 14 September 2026\, via the Fond
 s BJP subsidy portal. Online office hours on 8 September 2026\; questions 
 on 020 63 86 295.\n\nOrganisation: Fonds Bijzondere Journalistieke Project
 en (Fonds BJP)\nLocation: Netherlands\; for freelance journalists working 
 on Dutch regional and local reporting\nAward: Up to EUR 19\,200 for six mo
 nths of work on a single reporting dossier. No application fee.\nDuration:
  Six months of dedicated reporting on one subject area\n\nMore: https://ww
 w.fondsbjp.nl/subsidies/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=
 referral
URL:https://www.fondsbjp.nl/subsidies/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands\; for freelance journalists working on Dutch regional 
 and local reporting
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tartu-city-of-literature-residency-autumn-2026@artificialnouveau.github
 .io
DTSTAMP:20260824T105311Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Tartu UNESCO City of Literature Residency for Writers and
  Translators\, Autumn 2026
DESCRIPTION:The Estonian Literary Society\, which coordinates Tartu UNESCO 
 City of Literature\, runs an international residency programme for writers
  and translators that has hosted authors from Slovenia\, Ireland\, Hungary
 \, the USA\, the UK\, Ukraine and Canada since 2017. This is the open call
  for the autumn 2026 slot: one resident stays two months in the Karl Risti
 kivi residency apartment in Tartu\, working on their own writing or transl
 ation while connecting with the local literary scene. WHAT THE RESIDENCY O
 FFERS: a EUR 600 monthly stipend\, travel reimbursement up to EUR 350\, fr
 ee accommodation\, a local support coordinator to help arrange cultural en
 gagements\, and opportunities to perform and present at literary events. T
 he autumn period covers the interdisciplinary literary festival Crazy Tart
 u on 12 to 14 November\, and the resident is offered a slot to perform the
 re alongside writers\, poets\, musicians and artists from Estonia and abro
 ad. ELIGIBILITY: open to writers\, poets and translators of Estonian liter
 ature of any nationality\; applicants need an upper-intermediate level of 
 spoken English\, at least one published book\, screenplay\, theatre script
  or translation from Estonian into another language\, a demonstrable inter
 est in Estonian culture and literature\, a willingness to take part in loc
 al literary activities\, and a commitment to working on their own literary
  project during the stay. HOW TO APPLY: complete the online application fo
 rm linked from the residency page and upload a fragment of up to five page
 s of a published text (in Estonian or English) or of a published translati
 on. SELECTION: made by a committee representing the Estonian Literary Soci
 ety\, the Estonian Writers Union\, the Estonian Literary Museum and the Ta
 rtu Literature House Foundation. Results are announced before 15 September
  2026. The programme's stated aims are to enhance international exchange\,
  diversify the local literary scene\, introduce new foreign authors and th
 eir work to Estonian readers\, and build lasting connections beyond the re
 sidency period. Questions: Marja Unt\, eks@kirjandus.ee. Deadline 1 Septem
 ber 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Estonian Literary Society (Eesti Kirjanduse Sel
 ts)\, Focal Point for Tartu UNESCO City of Literature\nLocation: Tartu\, E
 stonia. Open to writers\, poets and translators of Estonian literature wor
 ldwide.\nAward: Monthly stipend of EUR 600 for the two-month stay (EUR 1\,
 200 in total)\, plus reimbursement of travel costs up to EUR 350. Free acc
 ommodation is provided in the Karl Ristikivi residency apartment\, which h
 as a bedroom\, living room\, kitchen\, bathroom and exhibition room. One r
 esident is selected. No application fee.\nDuration: Two months\, 15 Octobe
 r to 15 December 2026\, with some flexibility on exact dates\n\nMore: http
 s://tartu.kirjandus.ee/residency-autumn-2026?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://tartu.kirjandus.ee/residency-autumn-2026?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Tartu\, Estonia. Open to writers\, poets and translators of Estoni
 an literature worldwide.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:archipel-butor-livre-de-dialogue-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260824T105311Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260830
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260831
SUMMARY:Deadline: Archipel Butor Livre de dialogue Creation Residency 2027
DESCRIPTION:Archipel Butor runs its creation residency out of the former ho
 me of the writer Michel Butor in Lucinges\, Haute-Savoie\, and this call i
 s for a livre de dialogue\, a dialogue book made jointly by a writer and a
  visual artist. The residency exists to give a pair concentrated time to d
 evelop a book together and to raise the profile of artist book culture and
  of collaboration at the centre of artistic process. WHO APPLIES: a pair m
 ade up of an author with a project for a dialogue book and a visual artist
  collaborating on it. The two do not need to have worked together before\,
  but both must be present during the shared periods. WHAT IS PROVIDED: EUR
  2\,000 gross per month per artist\, up to two return trips per person wit
 hin France and Europe\, and accommodation in the writer's house. STRUCTURE
 : two months in total\, taken as eight weeks which may be split across the
  year from January 2027\, with 70 percent of the time given to creation an
 d 30 percent to mediation and public engagement activities. A videoconfere
 nce is held with the selected laureates beforehand to arrange on-site sche
 duling and the mediation sessions. HOW TO APPLY: follow the official call 
 document downloadable from the residency page\, submitting a single PDF to
  accueil@archipel-butor.fr containing a joint letter\, biographies of both
  practitioners\, the artistic proposal\, technical specifications and the 
 proposed mediation activities. NOTE: the call and application file are in 
 French. Deadline 30 August 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Archipel Butor\nLocation
 : Lucinges (74380)\, Haute-Savoie\, France\, in the house of the writer Mi
 chel Butor.\nAward: Creation grant of EUR 2\,000 gross per month per artis
 t\, so roughly EUR 4\,000 each across the two months and EUR 8\,000 for th
 e pair. Up to two return journeys per person are covered within France and
  Europe. Accommodation is provided in Michel Butor's writer's house. No ap
 plication fee.\nDuration: Two months in total\, taken as eight weeks that 
 may be split\, starting from January 2027. Time is split 70 percent creati
 on and 30 percent mediation activities.\n\nMore: https://www.archipel-buto
 r.fr/residence-creation/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=
 referral
URL:https://www.archipel-butor.fr/residence-creation/?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Lucinges (74380)\, Haute-Savoie\, France\, in the house of the wri
 ter Michel Butor.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:adagp-sgdl-arcane-grant-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260824T105311Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260908
SUMMARY:Deadline: Arcane Grant 2026 for Artist Books
DESCRIPTION:Artists' books get little support\, financially or in distribut
 ion\, despite their place in art history and in the careers of the people 
 who make them. ADAGP\, the French collecting society for copyright in the 
 visual arts\, and SGDL\, the French society of authors\, created the Arcan
 e grant in response: EUR 9\,000 to one winning project for the conception 
 and production of an artist's book made collaboratively by a visual artist
  and a writer. WHO CAN APPLY: a pair consisting of a professional visual a
 rtist from the French scene (working or residing in France for at least fi
 ve years\, or a French national living abroad) and a French-language autho
 r working in fiction\, non-fiction\, poetry\, children's literature or the
 atre who has already been published by a publisher. A trio is also possibl
 e where a publishing structure joins the project. WHAT COUNTS AS AN ARTIST
 'S BOOK: a creation\, a work of art in book form\, in a limited print run 
 of between 1 and 500 copies\, which may be signed or numbered. Explicitly 
 not eligible: magazines\, fanzines\, limited editions of an ordinary book\
 , and any publication that simply presents an artist's work\, such as mono
 graphs or illustrated books. APPLICATION: the file must be in French and i
 ncludes a jointly written project presentation of up to three pages coveri
 ng the artistic and editorial vision\, constituent elements\, methods of r
 ealisation and desired final form\; a one-page technical sheet giving titl
 e\, print run\, format\, page count\, paper quality\, printing techniques 
 and materials\; a provisional timetable\; and a detailed balanced provisio
 nal budget of expenses and financing. Artistic elements are a CV of exhibi
 tions and publications (2 pages) and a portfolio with website link (10 pag
 es) for the artist\, a CV and website link for the author (2 pages)\, and 
 a one-page editorial line for the publishing structure if there is one\; c
 ontact details must be omitted from these. Administrative elements are swo
 rn declarations that the project is a new creation with copyright held sol
 ely by the pair\, that the artist is from the French scene\, and\, if appl
 icable\, that the publishing structure undertakes to publish the work. Tem
 plates are downloadable from the Required Documents page. TIMELINE: call l
 aunched 7 July 2026\, applications close 7 September 2026 at 2pm\, jury me
 ets November 2026\, winner announced end of November 2026\, and the work m
 ust be published within two years of that announcement. The regulations mu
 st be read before applying\, and submitting an application constitutes acc
 eptance of them. Contact: arcane@adagp.fr.\n\nOrganisation: ADAGP and SGDL
  (Societe des Gens de Lettres)\nLocation: France. Open to a professional v
 isual artist from the French scene (working or residing in France for at l
 east five years\, or of French nationality living abroad) paired with a Fr
 ench-language author.\nAward: EUR 9\,000 to the single winning project\, s
 upporting the conception and production of an artist's book. NOTE ON TAX: 
 ADAGP grants count as primary artistic income under the French Intellectua
 l Property Code (art. L112-2)\, so the sum falls under the artist-author s
 ocial security and tax regime\, subject to URSSAF contributions and income
  tax declared as non-commercial profits (micro-BNC or controlled declarati
 on). VAT is not due. No application fee.\nDuration: The winning duo or tri
 o commits to publishing the artist's book within two years of the announce
 ment\n\nMore: https://candidatures.adagp.fr/en/?option=com_emundus&view=pr
 ogramme&cid=187&Itemid=1531&utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medi
 um=referral
URL:https://candidatures.adagp.fr/en/?option=com_emundus&view=programme&cid
 =187&Itemid=1531&utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:France. Open to a professional visual artist from the French scene
  (working or residing in France for at least five years\, or of French nat
 ionality living abroad) paired with a French-language author.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
